      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-09-16T08:49:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s because rustc doesn\u0027t yet support a Linux-based target using Bionic as lib. Following is the arm64/linux targets that are currently supported.\n\n$ prebuilts/rust/linux-x86/1.45.2/bin/rustc --print target-list | grep aarch64 | grep linux\naarch64-linux-android\naarch64-unknown-linux-gnu\naarch64-unknown-linux-musl\n\nYou might wonder why we don\u0027t use glibc (aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu). It was once attempted, but the amount of work required was too big. Please visit go/android-build-linux-cross for some more.",
      "parentUuid": "a8922418_54b6d4a5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 28,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 29,
        "endChar": 39
